why would the studio purposefully avoid  honoring one of its most popular star  wars characters with a stand-alone big  screen adventure  there's more than one reason as it turns  out here's why disney won't give  darth maul his own movie if you're not a  hardcore star wars fan you may be  surprised by the notion that maul  didn't die in the prequel trilogy there  are a lot of places you can go to find  the details of maul's story if you're  interested but suffice to say that it's  complicated  maul not only at one point builds  himself a bunch of legs out of trash  he later gets cybernetic legs that  mother talzin creates for him he goes on  to build a bunch of different crime  syndicates that serve various purposes  his backstory is rich but it's a story  that's already been told  so it may not make sense for it to be  retold in a feature film format  in order to tell a new story featuring  maul how would disney approach what he  has been through over the course of his  life  not all star wars fans have watched all  the animated series  or read all the comics and that could  impact both how understandable a mall  film would be  and interest in the film itself the best  way to approach a mall feature film  would likely be to tell the most  important parts of his life story up to  the point that a new story would take  place  depending on when in star wars history  that film was set  it could take quite a while to tell the  relevant bits of maul's history  that leaves less time for any new events  that would theoretically be the point of  the film  and that can be really complicated from  a storytelling standpoint  do fans want to sit through 30 minutes  of history that's accessible in other  formats to see an  hour or so of new content and on the  flip side  would that be accessible enough for new  viewers there's a fine line to walk  there that would likely have diminishing  returns for disney  it's easier for them to focus on  characters whose backstories are more  well-known  or create brand new characters that they  can establish on their terms  certainly a compelling story could be  told by rehashing all of maul's history  but is it worth disney's time and money  to do so  sure anti-heroes can be really  entertaining to watch there's no rule  that says that every movie  tv show comic or whatever has to have a  protagonist who is at least a little bit  good  but this is disney we're talking about  and they tend to like their leads to  not be completely on the side of  darkness maul's story while it's complex  and certainly adds depth to the  character  doesn't ever show him regretting the  things he's done and he continues to  harbor a lot of hate for a wide variety  of people across the star wars universe  throughout his life  especially the jedi it's possible to  tell a compelling backstory with this  character  absolutely but it may not have the  message that disney wishes to send  death and mayhem and fiction can be fun  to watch they just don't always endear  characters to fans  perhaps if maul had more redeeming  qualities it might be possible  but that's just not how the character  has been established and forcing that  into a movie seems antithetical to who  he is  in the history of the star wars  franchise there's never been a  villain-focused film  certainly villains are extremely  important to the universe and many of  them have captured imaginations  while some star wars villains have been  given their own books and comic series  they have never been placed at the  center of a film i was destined to  become  so much more boba fett came close but  that didn't pan out  given the good versus evil nature of the  main star wars stories  it's clear that they want you to root  for the good guys even if that's not  always how fans align  so of course as stewards of the  franchise disney seems unlikely to put  money  into featuring villains in their own  films while it's true that the prequel  trilogy focuses on anakin who becomes  darth vader  really he ceases to be the focus of the  story at the moment he does  at that point he's sidelined to being an  antagonist  if vader of all characters hasn't been  given his own film  why would maul it isn't all bad news for  maul fans though  it's been rumored that he may have  planned appearances in several upcoming  disney plus shows  including the live-action kenobi and the  animated series the bad batch  the character's appearance as a guest on  shows like these would give disney the  opportunity to use  maul without needing to delve into his  backstory to the degree they would for a  feature  film focused entirely on him the other  benefit of having maul appear on a tv  show instead of star in a feature film  is that bits and pieces of his backstory  could be explored without taking away  from the overall new content  if these rumors are true disney could be  trying to test out fan interest in the  character currently  but they wouldn't necessarily want to  over saturate their content with maul  it's also been rumored that maul could  be getting his very own disney plus  series  disney is likely determining the most  effective use of the character at this  point and if they go in the direction of  a tv show  which it seems they will it's less  likely they'll invest in a feature film  about him as well there would be no  point in double dipping that way  ultimately a tv series feels like a  better fit for the character given his  complex history and the challenges of  bringing that to a feature film  doing a show would allow disney to  explore that backstory at their leisure  while also telling a brand new story the  balance would still be very important  but it's much more manageable and longer  form storytelling  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite stuff are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  you
 

